    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0555" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg449"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received November 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1391.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a translation
                    of a communication from the foreign office to me of the 19th instant.</p>
                <p>I took occasion a few days ago to represent to the yamên that my advices were
                    that there was great danger of a riot at Wuchang, and to urge the necessity of
                    taking strong measures for the protection of the missionaries located there,
                    some of whom are Americans.</p>
                <p>It will be seen from the inclosure that the necessary orders have been
                    issued.</p>
                <p>We have no news of any riot since the one at Ichang.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d393-a1.xml" xpointer="d393-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
